{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZZg2S8ZqGZmu16sJUQC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis, I can see:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order.kt:11-16 — Order entity lacks a status field\n- OrderController.kt:17-46 — Has create, get, list but no cancel endpoint\n- ShipmentController.kt:26-44 — Creates shipments without checking order status\n- Shipment.kt:9-27 — Shipment already has status enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ApiError.kt:31-37 — ErrorCode enum defines the contract; currently has ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n\n**Conventions in this repository:**\n- Controllers throw ApiExceptions (ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409)\n- GlobalExceptionHandler centralizes error responses with ApiError envelope\n- Tests verify both HTTP status and error body structure with jsonPath\n- Tests reset repository in @BeforeEach\n- Repositories provide save(), existsById(), findById(), findAll(), clear()\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. Order.kt — must add OrderStatus enum and status field\n2. OrderController.kt — must add POST cancel endpoint; must inject ShipmentRepository to cancel shipments\n3. ShipmentController.kt — must reject shipment creation if order is CANCELLED\n4. ApiError.kt — must add error codes for cancel-specific conflicts\n5. OrderControllerTest.kt — must add tests for cancel behavior\n6. ShipmentRepository.kt — must add findByOrderId() to query shipments by order\n\n**Risks:**\n- Race condition if multiple cancel requests arrive simultaneously\n- Must ensure atomicity: check for CONFIRMED shipments before any changes\n- Shipment creation for cancelled order must be enforced everywhere\n\n**Open questions:** None — the ticket is explicit about the behavior and error codes.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Add `OrderStatus` enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and `status` field to Order data class. New orders default to ACTIVE.\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt** — Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String)` method to ShipmentRepository, or add a query method to find shipments for a given order.\n\n3. **ApiError.kt** — Add two new ErrorCode values:\n   - `ORDER_CANCEL_BLOCKED_BY_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` (for 409 when shipment is CONFIRMED)\n   - `SHIPMENT_CREATION_BLOCKED_ORDER_CANCELLED` (for 409 when order is CANCELLED)\n\n4. **OrderController.kt** — Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that:\n   - Returns 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND if order doesn't exist\n   - If order is already CANCELLED, succeeds and returns the order (idempotent)\n   - If any shipment is CONFIRMED, throws ConflictException with new error code and changes nothing\n   - Otherwise, sets order status to CANCELLED, saves it, cancels all CREATED shipments, and returns the order\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** — Before saving a new shipment, check if the order exists and is CANCELLED. If so, throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_CREATION_BLOCKED_ORDER_CANCELLED.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Add tests covering:\n   - Cancelling an ACTIVE order transitions it to CANCELLED and returns 200\n   - Cancelling an already CANCELLED order succeeds (idempotent)\n   - Cancelling an order with a CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 and changes nothing\n   - Cancelling a non-existent order returns 404\n   - After cancelling, CREATED shipments are cancelled but CONFIRMED ones remain unchanged\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:** Using a single generic \"CONFLICT\" error code for both cancel scenarios. Rejected because the ticket's API design follows the pattern of specific error codes (ORDER_NOT_FOUND vs SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND), so two specific codes maintain the contract clarity.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n- **Cancel ACTIVE order:** Read order (404 if missing), read all shipments for that order, check if any CONFIRMED (409 if found), set order status to CANCELLED, save order, for each CREATED shipment: set status to CANCELLED and save, return updated order with 200 OK\n- **Cancel already CANCELLED order:** Read order (404 if missing), order is already CANCELLED, skip shipment logic, return order with 200 OK (idempotent)\n- **Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment:** Read order (404 if missing), read shipments, find CONFIRMED (throw 409), no changes made, response body includes error code\n- **Create shipment for CANCELLED order:** Read order (404 if missing), check status, if CANCELLED throw 409, otherwise create shipment\n\n**Test strategy:**\n1. `cancel ACTIVE order` — creates order, cancels it, verifies status is CANCELLED and returns 200\n2. `cancel already CANCELLED order succeeds` — cancels twice, second cancel succeeds (idempotent)\n3. `cancel with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 and changes nothing` — creates order, creates shipment, confirms it, attempts cancel, verifies 409, verifies order still ACTIVE\n4. `cancel non-existent order returns 404` — attempts to cancel unknown order\n5. `create shipment for CANCELLED order returns 409` — cancels order, attempts to create shipment, verifies 409\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the design. Starting with Order.kt to add status:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":772,"cache_read_input_tokens":21054,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":772},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e352c2c4-67b5-4978-a762-f81fbeafe387","uuid":"0cbf46a1-cdb4-4966-9372-591bbcd7fb38","timestamp":"2026-09-30T11:43:15.650Z","request_id":"req_011CfZZg23p77eLNAf5BUBjK"}
