{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZZoy4x98oScquaipCBp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Command:** `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/` directory\n\n**Result:** SUCCESS\n- All 23 tests passed (0 failures, 0 errors)\n- OrderControllerTest: 12 tests (baseline 5 + new 7 tests for cancel functionality)\n- ShipmentControllerTest: 7 tests (baseline 5 + new 2 tests for cancelled order blocking)\n- Full module tests passed on first run\n\n**Failures:** None\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** — `./mvnw test` completed successfully with BUILD SUCCESS\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** — All baseline tests (5 in OrderControllerTest, 5 in ShipmentControllerTest) pass without modification\n3. ✅ **`POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` cancels active order, persists, and cancels CREATED shipments** — Tested by:\n   - `cancels an ACTIVE order and transitions it to CANCELLED` — verifies order.status becomes CANCELLED\n   - `GET the cancelled order reflects the CANCELLED status` — verifies persistence via GET\n   - `cancelling an order cancels its CREATED shipments` — directly verifies shipment status change\n4. ✅ **Error responses consistent with rest of API** — All errors use ApiException/ConflictException thrown to GlobalExceptionHandler, follow same envelope pattern (code, message, fields)\n5. ✅ **Repeated cancel succeeds, confirmed shipment blocks, unknown order 404, shipment for cancelled order 409:**\n   - `cancelling an already CANCELLED order succeeds and is idempotent` — idempotent retry\n   - `cancelling an order with a CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 and changes nothing` — blocks with specific error code, verifies no state change\n   - `cancelling a non-existent order returns 404` — correct status and error code\n   - `rejects shipment creation for a CANCELLED order with 409` — correct status and error code\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency** — No changes to pom.xml, only added Kotlin code\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** — Only modified Order.kt, OrderController.kt, ShipmentController.kt, ApiError.kt, ShipmentRepository.kt, and added test methods\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Added `OrderStatus` enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and `status` field with default ACTIVE. Required for feature.\n\n2. **ApiError.kt** — Added two error codes: `ORDER_CANCEL_BLOCKED_BY_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` and `SHIPMENT_CREATION_BLOCKED_ORDER_CANCELLED`. Required for specific error contract.\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Added `findByOrderId(orderId: String)` method to query shipments for an order. Required for cancel endpoint to find shipments to update.\n\n4. **OrderController.kt** — \n   - Injected `InMemoryShipmentRepository` \n   - Added `cancel(@PathVariable orderId: String)` endpoint\n   - Handles 404 for missing order\n   - Returns order without change if already CANCELLED (idempotent)\n   - Checks for CONFIRMED shipments and throws 409 if found\n   - Sets order status to CANCELLED and saves\n   - Cancels all CREATED shipments\n   - Required for feature\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** — \n   - Injected `InMemoryOrderRepository`\n   - Added check in create endpoint: if order exists and is CANCELLED, throws 409\n   - Maintains existing behavior if order doesn't exist\n   - Required to enforce constraint that cancelled orders cannot have new shipments\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — \n   - Added 7 new test methods covering all cancel scenarios\n   - Tests verify both status codes and error response bodies\n   - All pass\n   - Required for verification\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — \n   - Added 2 new test methods: one for rejected shipment creation on cancelled order, one verifying non-existent order still works\n   - All pass\n   - Required for verification\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All criteria implemented.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\n**Requirement:** Add order cancellation endpoint that transitions ACTIVE orders to CANCELLED, cancels CREATED shipments, blocks if any shipment is CONFIRMED, allows idempotent retries, rejects 404 for unknown orders and 409 for cancelled orders receiving shipments.\n\n**Changed:**\n- Order.kt — Added OrderStatus enum and status field to Order\n- ApiError.kt — Added two new ErrorCode values for cancel-specific conflicts\n- ShipmentRepository.kt — Added findByOrderId() method to query shipments by order\n- OrderController.kt — Added POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with full logic\n- ShipmentController.kt — Added validation to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders\n- OrderControllerTest.kt — Added 7 tests covering all cancel scenarios\n- ShipmentControllerTest.kt — Added 2 tests for cancelled order shipment blocking\n\n**Tests:**\n- `newly created order has ACTIVE status` — Verifies default status is ACTIVE\n- `cancels an ACTIVE order and transitions it to CANCELLED` — Verifies cancel transitions order to CANCELLED\n- `GET the cancelled order reflects the CANCELLED status` — Verifies persistence of status change\n- `cancelling an already CANCELLED order succeeds and is idempotent` — Verifies retry safety\n- `cancelling a non-existent order returns 404` — Verifies 404 response for missing order\n- `cancelling an order cancels its CREATED shipments` — Verifies CREATED shipments are cancelled\n- `cancelling an order with a CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 and changes nothing` — Verifies blocking and all-or-nothing semantics\n- `cancelling an order with multiple shipments cancels only CREATED ones` — Verifies selective cancellation\n- `rejects shipment creation for a CANCELLED order with 409` — Verifies shipment creation is blocked\n- `allows shipment creation for non-existent order` — Verifies existing behavior preserved\n\n**Verification:** `./mvnw test` completed with BUILD SUCCESS, 23 tests passed, 0 failures\n\n**Not done:** Nothing. All acceptance criteria satisfied, all tests pas